From dffbe61c616cfb395b6dec2e3f4f431d63c05ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:56:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Require a whole hdr_extend in
 HDR_EXT_DATA

The HDR_EXT_DATA blob is set with no size check, but the commit path
casts its data to struct hdr_extend and reads whichever union member
hdr_type names: the DOVI LUTs, the HDR Vivid tables, the dynamic
metadata. A shorter blob makes the VOP read past its end into the slab
and program whatever it finds there.

Check the length as ACM_LUT_DATA and POST_CSC_DATA already do, so a
blob must carry the whole struct and unused tail is zeroes. Rockchip's
own parser library sends 3108 bytes, the HDR Vivid registers without the
dynamic metadata the commit still reads; those blobs are now refused.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
index 2d74ccc..68eaef3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -17094,7 +17094,7 @@ static int vop2_crtc_atomic_set_property(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 		ret = vop2_atomic_replace_property_blob_from_id(drm_dev,
 								&vcstate->hdr_ext_data,
 								val,
-								-1, -1,
+								sizeof(struct hdr_extend), -1,
 								&replaced);
 		return ret;
 	}
